#: ../../tools/proteinsplus_tools.rst:154 88c4ade1c18f41a2adcf16c79b3c1cdb
msgid ""
"Predict druggable binding sites using DoGSite3 algorithm with ligand-"
"biased grid option. Enhanced..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/proteinsplus_tools.rst 6c1ce6b392ad442bb1c645bf317de792
msgid "ProteinsPlus_predict_binding_sites_v3 tool specification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/proteinsplus_tools.rst:160 734a0b63ce8e433292ba94f8e5cb16db
msgid "**Name**: ``ProteinsPlus_predict_binding_sites_v3``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/proteinsplus_tools.rst:162 a1152a5ece8749f88863a941dbee6752
msgid ""
"**Description**: Predict druggable binding sites using DoGSite3 algorithm"
" with ligand-biased grid option. Enhanced version of DoGSiteScorer with "
"improved binding site detection. Input can be a PDB ID with optional "
"reference ligand for biased grid calculations. Returns predicted pockets "
"with druggability scores, geometric properties, and detailed subpocket "
"analysis. Supports ligand-based grid biasing to focus predictions around "
"known binding sites. Useful for comprehensive binding site "
"characterization and structure-based drug design workflows. Example: "
"Analyze 1KZK with ligand JE2\\_A\\_701 to identify druggable sites near "
"the co-crystallized ligand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/proteinsplus_tools.rst:172 6499128d37b042698560ef49bbdeb569
msgid ""
"``ligand`` (string) (optional) Reference ligand identifier in format "
"'residue\\_name\\_residue\\_chain\\_residue\\_number' (e.g., "
"'JE2\\_A\\_701'). Optional - used for ligand-biased grid calculations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/proteinsplus_tools.rst:175 5e5fa133c0a7467daaac780b06d2b879
msgid ""
"``ligand_bias`` (boolean) (optional) Enable ligand-biased grid "
"calculations (true) or standard detection (false). Requires ligand "
"parameter. Default: false. Example: Use true to focus detection around "
"known binding site."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/proteinsplus_tools.rst:178 bbd77e5b083745d3a5257fb1452bc1c9
msgid ""
"``analysis_detail`` (string) (optional) Analysis level: '0' for pockets "
"only (faster), '1' for pockets and subpockets (comprehensive). Default: "
"'1'. Example: Use '1' for detailed analysis, '0' for quick screening."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/proteinsplus_tools.rst:181 2fca8bf545e4431e9a63e0b39a6581f1
msgid ""
"``druggability`` (string) (optional) Prediction granularity: '0' for "
"geometric properties only, '1' for properties and druggability scores. "
"Default: '1'. Example: Use '1' for drug discovery (includes "
"druggability), '0' for structure analysis only."
msgstr ""

